  "notes": "projectVersion at this commit: 4.10.17-SNAPSHOT. The nine modules are the micronaut-core modules that micronaut-http-server brings onto the class path. The build compiles the annotation processors it needs from the same tree (micronaut-core-processor, -inject-java, -graal) and runs them over context, context-propagation (kapt), http, router and http-server, so bean definitions and introspections come from the commit's own processors. Gradle's dependency substitution maps io.micronaut:micronaut-* to the projects being built; the only io.micronaut artifacts fetched are BOM POMs and separate Micronaut projects used at build time only (micronaut-build plugins, docs, sourcegen, validation, rxjava2/3, runtime-groovy). Flags: --no-build-cache keeps Gradle from taking compiled outputs from a build cache (gradle.properties sets org.gradle.caching=true); -Pkotlin.compiler.execution.strategy=in-process avoids a separate Kotlin daemon; -x test, --max-workers=2 and the heap are resource flags. Fixed: the nine artifacts at 4.10.17."
